From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] There is no AUR on MSYS2

The AUR is Arch Linux's user repository: its recipes are arch=('x86_64')
Linux, built by Arch's makepkg against glibc and installed by Arch's pacman.
MSYS2 has no equivalent -- the extra packages here come from sync repositories
libalpm already reads -- and no AUR helper runs on it. So the AUR button on
the toolbar, between Cancel and the search bar, has nothing to offer.

It is only there by accident. The configured AUR tool defaults to the
DO_NOT_USE_AUR sentinel, so m_hasForeignTool starts false and initToolBar()
leaves the button out; then refreshToolBar() reads "no helper on a system that
is neither KaOS nor Parabola" as a user who uninstalled theirs and puts the
button back. getLinuxDistro() cannot say otherwise: it looks for
/etc/os-release, which patch 0007 deliberately does not translate, finds
nothing, and returns its uninitialised static -- ectn_ARCHBANGLINUX.

Clicking it reaches the one branch of AURToolSelected() that is live while
getAvailableAURTools() holds nothing but the sentinel: an offer to curl the
latest yay release from GitHub into ~/.config/octopi, untar it, symlink it and
run it. That is a Linux ELF binary, and the commands around it are
untranslated POSIX paths, so nothing comes of it -- a dead button promising
something that would be harmful if it worked.

The Options page goes with it: a helper to pick, an AUR build directory, and
an aur.archlinux.org login to vote with. The distros that have no AUR already
hide that page, so this hides it the same way -- and leaves its widgets
unloaded, which is why accept() must stop saving them. Every one of them would
otherwise compare unequal to its stored setting and write an empty value back,
clearing an AUR build directory and warning about a restart on each OK.

What stays: foreign packages are what pacman -Qm reports, not what an AUR
helper installed, so they are still listed and marked. Only the
foreign-outdated variant of that mark goes with the flag.

Not for upstream: meaningless where there is an AUR to reach.
diff --git a/src/mainwindow_refresh.cpp b/src/mainwindow_refresh.cpp
index db8986b..0bd1eeb 100644
--- a/src/mainwindow_refresh.cpp
+++ b/src/mainwindow_refresh.cpp
@@ -1327,6 +1327,14 @@
   m_hasForeignTool =
       UnixCommand::hasTheExecutable(Package::getForeignRepositoryToolName());

+  // MSYS2 has no AUR. The fallback below reads "an Arch-based system with no
+  // helper installed" as a user who lost theirs and puts the AUR button back
+  // on the toolbar, and all that button can then do is offer to download yay
+  // -- a Linux binary that builds Arch packages. Leaving m_hasForeignTool
+  // false keeps it off, and with it Ctrl+Shift+Y, Ctrl+Shift+O, the
+  // help-usage line and the AUR context-menu actions, which are gated on the
+  // same flag.
+#ifndef Q_OS_WIN
   //If there's no AUR helper installed let's check if we are running an ARCH based OS
   if (!m_hasForeignTool)
   {
@@ -1340,6 +1348,7 @@
       SettingsManager::setAURTool(ctn_NO_AUR_TOOL);
     }
   }
+#endif

   if (m_hasForeignTool)
   {
diff --git a/src/optionsdialog.cpp b/src/optionsdialog.cpp
index 1ba906c..3873764 100644
--- a/src/optionsdialog.cpp
+++ b/src/optionsdialog.cpp
@@ -317,6 +317,15 @@
  */
 void OptionsDialog::initAURTab()
 {
+#ifdef Q_OS_WIN
+  // The page picks an AUR helper, an AUR build directory and an
+  // aur.archlinux.org login, none of which mean anything here. Hidden the way
+  // the distros without an AUR hide it below, and left unloaded, which is why
+  // accept() must not save it either.
+  removeTabByName(QStringLiteral("AUR"));
+  return;
+#endif
+
   cbSearchOutdatedAURPackages->setChecked(SettingsManager::getSearchOutdatedAURPackages());

   gbAURVoting->setStyleSheet(QStringLiteral("border:none"));
@@ -700,6 +709,11 @@
     ColumnsChanged = true;
   }

+  // Nothing to save: initAURTab() never loaded these widgets on Windows, so
+  // every one of them would compare unequal to the stored setting and write
+  // an empty value back -- clearing a build directory, and warning about a
+  // restart on each OK.
+#ifndef Q_OS_WIN
   //Set AUR Tool...
   if (UnixCommand::getLinuxDistro() != ectn_KAOS ||
       UnixCommand::getLinuxDistro() != ectn_PARABOLA)
@@ -844,6 +858,7 @@
       QMessageBox::warning(this, StrConstants::getWarning(), StrConstants::getWarnNeedsAppRestart());
     }
   }
+#endif

   //Set icon...
   if (!cbUseDefaultIcons->isChecked())
